<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event</p><h1 class="enc-title">Eleutheria (Plataea)</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Eleutheria was a festival of freedom held at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-plataea">Plataea</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boeotia">Boeotia</a> in honour of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zeus">Zeus</a> Eleutherios, commemorating the Greek victory over the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persians">Persians</a> there in 479 BCE. Celebrated every four years with games, including a race in armour, it was accompanied by yearly rites at the graves of the fallen, which the Plataeans were charged to tend. It continued into Roman times.</p></div>
